# Input
```ts
/* should generate diagnostics */
new Date((date as Date).getTime());
new Date((date satisfies Date).getTime());
new Date(date!.getTime());

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid.ts:2:25 lint/nursery/noUselessDateGetTime  FIXABLE  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ! This .getTime() call is unnecessary.
  
    1 │ /* should generate diagnostics */
  > 2 │ new Date((date as Date).getTime());
      │                         ^^^^^^^^^
    3 │ new Date((date satisfies Date).getTime());
    4 │ new Date(date!.getTime());
  
  i Passing a date directly to new Date() already creates a copy of it.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  
  i Unsafe fix: Remove the .getTime() call.
  
    2 │ new·Date((date·as·Date).getTime());
      │                        ----------  

```

